# Mada AMS — reverse proxy with automatic HTTPS (Caddy)
# --------------------------------------------------------------
# Put AMS behind a real domain name that people just type and sign in.
# Caddy gets and renews a free HTTPS certificate automatically.
#
# 1) Edit the domain below to yours.
# 2) Run AMS headless on the same machine, listening on 127.0.0.1:8080:
#       Windows : set ITAM_NO_BROWSER=1 && set PORT=8080 && ITAM.exe
#       Linux   : ITAM_NO_BROWSER=1 PORT=8080 python run_server.py
# 3) Start Caddy in this folder:  caddy run
#
# --- PUBLIC: reachable from anywhere, incl. off-campus --------------
# Requires: a DNS A record  itam.madaacademy.edu.jo -> your school's
# public IP, and the router/firewall forwarding ports 80 and 443 to
# this server. Caddy fetches a trusted Let's Encrypt certificate.

itam.madaacademy.edu.jo {
    encode zstd gzip
    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
}

# --- INTERNAL only: same name, school network only ------------------
# If AMS should only work inside the school (no ports opened to the
# internet), comment out the block above and use ONE of these instead.
# Point INTERNAL DNS  itam.madaacademy.edu.jo -> the server's LAN IP.
#
# Real trusted HTTPS without exposing ports (DNS-01 challenge). Needs a
# Caddy build with your DNS provider's plugin and an API token:
# itam.madaacademy.edu.jo {
#     tls { dns <your-dns-provider> {env.DNS_API_TOKEN} }
#     reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
# }
#
# Or a self-signed local certificate (staff click through / install once):
# itam.madaacademy.edu.jo {
#     tls internal
#     reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
# }
#
# Or plain HTTP on the LAN (simplest, no certificate):
# http://itam.madaacademy.edu.jo {
#     reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
# }
